course: dictionary
lesson: 13700
title: Insert: put it in
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To insert something means to put it into something else. «Insert the key into the lock» means push the key inside the lock. Insert is a doing word, so it is a verb.
explain: You can also insert words, pictures or numbers into a text or a list. «Insert a picture after the first paragraph» means add the picture between the paragraphs. The new thing goes in the middle of what is already there.
explain: Look at the words around insert to find its meaning. If a sign says «Insert a coin», it wants you to push a coin into a slot. Try your meaning in the sentence: does "put in" still make sense? Then you have it.
explain: Insert can also be a noun, meaning an extra page or piece put inside something. «The magazine had a free insert inside: a leaflet about bikes.» Here the insert is the extra leaflet.
fact: Insert means to put something into something else.
fact: Insert can be a verb (to insert, I insert, I inserted) or a noun (an insert).
fact: In writing you can insert a word, a sentence or a picture into a text.
fact: In maths you insert the missing number or a sign, such as + or −, into a number sentence.
fact: An insert is an extra page or piece put inside something, like a leaflet in a magazine.
exercise: «Please insert a coin to start the machine.» What does insert mean here? | Take the coin out | *Put the coin into the machine | Count the coins | Throw the coin away
exercise: In «8 ? 2 = 10», what could you insert in place of the question mark to make it true? | 10 | 8 | *+ | 2
exercise: Tom wants to insert a picture into his story. What is he doing? | Taking the picture out of his story | Painting the cover of his book | Printing his story in colour | *Adding the picture into his story
test: «The magazine had a free insert inside.» What is an insert? | *An extra page or piece put inside something | A type of cover | A kind of pen | A long word
test: Which sentence uses insert as a verb? | The insert was bright and colourful | *Please insert the missing number | The magazine had a free insert | Inserts are fun to read
exam: Which word means to put words or pictures into a text? | Cut | *Insert | Print | Delete
